C1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"a6e0bf7fb44a00434b4fee13701253971d39af3f99ebca4956d6409509c37ac3","event_uuid":"67b49bab-1709-4d95-89ca-f0df0a972d96","position":{"commit_sha":"8181932fd37923a231c680058b3a9c565e7bbf46","position":"1785772330810326001-67b49bab-1709-4d95-89ca-f0df0a972d96"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented + pushed as Gerrit change 1291 (commit 4479477577). All three prose blocks landed: (14) four writebacks + approval-gate own-tracker carve-out; (15) Step 7 two-axis with OR trigger + 4-question parity census (5-slot channel checklist, forced artifacts); (16) Reporting residual-risk disposition item. Validation: test_skill_shared_sync.py 5/5 green (SKILL.md not in synced set — no perturbation); no AGENTS.md references (discovered_from stated inline at both filing points); dry-run of the census against the 4b59 link-direction class: NAME THE RULE = 'link direction (inward/outward) must translate consistently store<->Jira' (no site named); CENSUS flags dual-direction slot as the parity signature (outbound mapping vs inbound differ) — matching 4b59's actual history where the sibling lived on the mirror direction. Awaiting LLM-Review + Verified.","timestamp":1785772330810326001}],"created_at":1785640176607679001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"aefe2c5d-f645-48f3-b17b-90f30837ee47","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ad0d-6338-bc8c-43b6"},{"link_uuid":"e2740c96-b3de-42e6-97a4-113a7dbbfd45","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"4b54-6e28-45f7-42db"},{"link_uuid":"bae5d8ce-18de-4478-a54f-8d8c23678a82","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"3835-0fd6-b98c-47fa"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nThe debug skill reads prior tickets but never writes back (reads from a well it never fills); Step 7 sweeps by construct only (parity siblings are ABSENCES invisible to grep); Reporting lets residual fragility evaporate. Approved changes 14+15+16 from the bug-trend review.\n\n## Approach\n(14) Writebacks: Phase-1-exit RCA comment (root cause + discriminating evidence); Reporting summary comment (cause/proof/test/fix/siblings/replication); not-a-bug classification comment + cited source; Step-7 siblings filed via create + discovered_from encoded DIRECTLY in the skill (no AGENTS.md reference — client projects may lack it). Tracker discriminator, stated inline in the skill: the tracker the debug session is already operating within — the one that produced or holds the ticket under debug — is \"the project's own mandated tracker\" and receives the prescribed writebacks un-gated; ANY other tracker is third-party and stays approval-gated. The existing approval-gate paragraph (SKILL.md \"Seek explicit user approval… writing/transitioning/commenting on Jira or other trackers\") is explicitly amended in the same change with a carve-out sentence so the prescribed own-tracker writebacks do not contradict it; all other tracker mutations remain gated. (15) Step 7 second sweep axis (construct search unchanged), decomposed into 4 forced-artifact questions: NAME THE RULE (operation+property, must not name the fixed site); CHANNEL CENSUS (fixed 5-slot checklist: CLI / MCP-API / library-facade / automated-callers / dual-direction, plus caller-set derivation — a surface absent from the shared core's callers is the parity signature); PER-SURFACE PROBE (cite path:line or MISSING); DISPOSITION (RED-test fix or ticket + discovered_from). Step 7's entry trigger is amended to the OR of the two axis triggers: enter when the root cause is a repeatable construct pattern (axis 1, existing wording) OR when the fixed code sits on one of several parallel surfaces (axis 2 — a parity sibling is an absence, present even for one-off constructs); each axis then runs only under its own condition. (16) Reporting item 'Residual risk & prevention': per observed-with-citation fragility, forced disposition — ticket filed (may propose structural guard) / accepted with reason / fixed in scope; 'none observed' legitimate; prose only, no new ticket-system structures.\n\n## Scope\n- examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md (single real file; ~35-45 lines total). SKILL.md has no symlink or synced copy — only shared/test-design.md is cp-synced across skills, and that file is untouched here.\n\n## Testing\nProse-only skill change: no code tests. Validation = the existing skill sync gate (tests/unit/test_skill_shared_sync.py, which covers shared/test-design.md only) run as a regression check confirming this change does not perturb the synced set, and a dry-run read-through against the 4-question artifacts on one historical bug (4b59 link-direction class).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] All four writebacks encoded at their lifecycle points, with the inline own-tracker-vs-third-party discriminator AND the approval-gate paragraph amended with the matching carve-out (no contradiction between the two sections).\n- [ ] Step 7 carries both axes with the 4-question decomposition and forced artifacts, and its entry trigger is the OR of the two axis conditions.\n- [ ] Reporting carries the residual-risk disposition item with 'none observed' legitimate.\n- [ ] No references to AGENTS.md; discovered_from linkage stated inline.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"examples/agent-skills/rebar-debug/SKILL.md","reason":"writebacks + two-axis sweep + residual-risk prose"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97"],["relates_to","3835-0fd6-b98c-47fa"],["relates_to","4b54-6e28-45f7-42db"],["relates_to","ad0d-6338-bc8c-43b6"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","parent_status_uuid":"fd1c5a9d-4353-42f0-9d58-42c8a4771670","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["skills"],"ticket_id":"78f1-13e8-7025-42ce","ticket_type":"story","title":"rebar-debug skill: ticket writebacks, two-axis Step-7 sweep, residual-risk disposition","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0f0c4c71-5b87-4a5f-9fb2-14c4924e92ea","aefe2c5d-f645-48f3-b17b-90f30837ee47","fa09941c-eabf-4699-8859-2d45445b6aa4","e2740c96-b3de-42e6-97a4-113a7dbbfd45","ed774925-5e20-40e7-a9d1-fe19db89423a","ac40aea5-b6ec-4b1e-90ab-78beba249d9b","fd1c5a9d-4353-42f0-9d58-42c8a4771670","08682a2c-3c7c-4313-8b65-17c350591c9c","67b49bab-1709-4d95-89ca-f0df0a972d96","bae5d8ce-18de-4478-a54f-8d8c23678a82"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785772478817761972,"uuid":"8883c732-e5f7-4399-a145-454ae03aa707"}